{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["occ"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"@interface"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNPolyline"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MLNMultiPoint","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)MLNMultiPoint","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPoint"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/LineOnUserTap","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/AnimatedLineExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GeoJSON","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Predicates_and_Expressions"]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add polyline shapes to the map by adding them to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object. Configure the appearance of an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"text":"’s or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s polylines collectively using an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNLineStyleLayer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNSymbolStyleLayer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object. To access a polyline’s attributes, use an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolylineFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, you can add a polyline overlay directly to a map view using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/addAnnotation:"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/addOverlay:","isActive":true},{"text":" methods. Configure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a polyline overlay’s appearance using","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapViewDelegate\/mapView:strokeColorForShapeAnnotation:"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapViewDelegate\/mapView:lineWidthForPolylineAnnotation:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are automatically connected in the order in which you provide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. The first and last vertices are not connected to each other, but you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D"},{"type":"text","text":" as the first and last vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order to close the polyline. To fill the space within the shape, use an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"type":"text","text":" object. To group multiple polylines together in one shape, use an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollection"},{"type":"text","text":" object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To make the polyline go across the antimeridian or international date line,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify some longitudes less than −180 degrees or greater than 180 degrees."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, a polyline that stretches from Tokyo to San Francisco would have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinates of (35.68476, -220.24257) and (37.78428, -122.41310)."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let coordinates = [","    CLLocationCoordinate2D(latitude: 35.68476, longitude: -220.24257),","    CLLocationCoordinate2D(latitude: 37.78428, longitude: -122.41310)","]","let polyline = MLNPolyline(coordinates: coordinates, count: UInt(coordinates.count))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A polyline is known as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LineString"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry in GeoJSON."}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","anchor":"Related-examples","text":"Related examples"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/LineOnUserTap","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/AnimatedLineExample","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"ide